CASCADE — licensing
===================

This repository contains material under two different licences. Which one
applies depends on the file, and the difference matters: one of them
carries a share-alike obligation.

  Source code, prompts, and documentation        MIT (below)
      everything under cascade/, tests/, scripts/, calibration/,
      prompts/, run.py, and the README files.

  Derived from MVTec LOCO AD                     CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
      masks/*.json.gz          instance masks computed from the images
      examples/*/scaffold.png  a scaffold drawn on one of the images

      These are derivative works of a dataset published under
      Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0, so they
      inherit that licence in full: attribution required, non-commercial
      use only, and anything derived from them must be shared alike.
      They are NOT covered by the MIT licence below.

          Bergmann, Batzner, Fauser, Sattlegger and Steger,
          "Beyond Dents and Scratches: Logical Constraints in
          Unsupervised Anomaly Detection and Localization",
          International Journal of Computer Vision, 2022.
          https://www.mvtec.com/company/research/datasets/mvtec-loco

      The dataset images themselves are not redistributed here; see
      scripts/download_mvtec_loco.py.

  Constraint text                                quoted, with citation
      constraints/logicqa_bullets.json reproduces the normality
      definitions published in LogicQA, verbatim and unaltered, so that
      every method is evaluated on the same constraint wording.

          Kwon et al., "LogicQA: Logical Anomaly Detection with
          Vision Language Model Generated Questions",
          ACL 2025 Industry Track.
          https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-industry.29.pdf


